│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model’s signal collapses in validation       │
│                          │ because the current feature set leans too heavily on long-horizon, regime-specific        │
│                          │ levels. I’m switching the feature bank toward shorter lookbacks and rolling z-score /     │
│                          │ rank normalization so the inputs become more regime-invariant. I also add a few explicit  │
│                          │ rate-of-change features for volatility, efficiency, and autocorrelation so the model can  │
│                          │ learn when market character is changing rather than only its absolute state.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, I reduce tree complexity and increase regularization / sample          │
│                          │ constraints to discourage memorizing brittle training-only patterns. I also lower the     │
│                          │ clipping threshold slightly to reduce outlier dominance while keeping enough dynamic      │
│                          │ range to avoid prediction collapse.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The intent is to raise validation slope and predicted dispersion without inflating        │
│                          │ train/val gap, while keeping feature count safely under the limit.                        │
