│                          │ regime because many current features encode absolute market levels over long windows,     │
│                          │ which are brittle under regime shift. I replace several long-horizon, level-based signals │
│                          │ with shorter-horizon and rolling z-scored versions that are more regime-invariant.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - use 5–20 bar windows more heavily, with fewer 60+ bar dependencies                      │
│                          │ - add rolling z-score normalization for returns, volatility, volume, and price-location   │
│                          │ features                                                                                  │
│                          │ - add short-term trend/volatility/efficiency change features, which capture the rate of   │
│                          │ change of market character                                                                │
│                          │ - keep feature count comfortably below 80                                                 │
│                          │ - preserve past-only computation and low runtime                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also modestly reduce model complexity and add regularization to improve cross-regime    │
│                          │ generalization and reduce prediction collapse.                                            │
