│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_shift_features                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model learns train-regime-specific slopes    │
│                          │ that vanish in validation. I’m making two coordinated changes:                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Hyperparameters:                                                                       │
│                          │    - Reduce excessive damping that is likely collapsing predictions toward the mean.      │
│                          │    - Use a slightly deeper but more regularized tree setup with more estimators and a     │
│                          │ lower learning rate, which usually helps XGBoost recover slope without overfitting as     │
│                          │ badly.                                                                                    │
│                          │    - Relax target clipping a bit so the model can still learn tail sensitivity.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Features:                                                                              │
│                          │    - Add more regime-invariant, rolling z-scored signals on very short windows.           │
│                          │    - Add explicit “character change” features: volatility trend, efficiency trend,        │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend.                                                                    │
│                          │    - Add a momentum × volatility-regime interaction, which often generalizes better than  │
│                          │ raw momentum alone across regime shifts.                                                  │
│                          │    - Keep the feature count comfortably under 80 and use only past data.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to increase val slope and prediction dispersion while preserving or improving │
│                          │ DA.                                                                                       │
