│ patch_name               │ regime_invariant_short_lookbacks                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the core failure mode: the model’s slope collapses out-of-sample        │
│                          │ because it is over-relying on regime-specific absolute levels that do not persist into    │
│                          │ the validation period. I’m making the feature set more regime-invariant by emphasizing    │
│                          │ short lookbacks, rolling z-scores, and “change in market character” features (volatility  │
│                          │ trend, efficiency trend, autocorrelation proxy trend). I’m also adding a compact          │
│                          │ momentum×volatility interaction, which often survives regime shifts better than           │
│                          │ standalone raw momentum or raw volatility.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, I’m slightly increasing expressivity while keeping regularization      │
│                          │ moderate: more trees with a smaller learning rate, shallower depth, and lower             │
│                          │ min_child_weight than the current setup. This should help recover validation slope and    │
│                          │ prediction dispersion without pushing train/val gap too far.                              │
