│ patch_description        │ The redesign restructures the feature engineering into modular logical blocks that        │
│                          │ prioritize regime-invariance through aggressive rolling Z-score normalization. By         │
│                          │ standardizing momentum, volatility, and volume features within short windows (5-30 bars), │
│                          │ the model is forced to learn how current market behavior relates to its immediate past    │
│                          │ rather than absolute levels, which often shift between market regimes. The XGBoost        │
│                          │ configuration is also adjusted: depth is increased to 4 and regularization is reduced to  │
│                          │ combat the 'magnitude collapse' (slope collapse) observed in previous iterations,         │
│                          │ allowing the model to produce predictions with higher variance and better scaling         │
│                          │ relative to the actual price movements.                                                   │
