│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model has enough fit on train/test, but its  │
│                          │ predictive slope collapses in the most recent regime. I’m making the feature set more     │
│                          │ regime-invariant and more sensitive to changes in market character by:                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - shifting several long lookbacks down to shorter horizons                                │
│                          │ - adding rolling z-scores for price/volatility/momentum so the model sees relative state, │
│                          │ not raw level                                                                             │
│                          │ - adding explicit “change in regime” features like volatility trend, efficiency trend,    │
│                          │ and autocorrelation trend                                                                 │
│                          │ - adding a simple momentum × volatility interaction that often survives regime shifts     │
│                          │ better than either component alone                                                        │
│                          │ - slightly loosening the model regularization and reducing tree count so XGBoost can keep │
│                          │ some expressivity without overfitting too hard                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help recover val slope and pred_std_ratio while keeping the train→val gap     │
│                          │ controlled.                                                                               │
